      {"id":15102465,"title":"Dutch Pharmacogenetics Working Group Guidelines November 2018","_sameAs":"https://api.pharmgkb.org/v1/preview/download/file/attachment/DPWG_November_2018.pdf","crossReferences":[{"id":1450415575,"resource":"URL","resourceId":"https://api.pharmgkb.org/v1/preview/download/file/attachment/DPWG_November_2018.pdf","_url":"https://api.pharmgkb.org/v1/preview/download/file/attachment/DPWG_November_2018.pdf"}],"objCls":"Literature","terms":[],"type":"Literature"}
    ],
    "otherPrescribingGuidance" : true,
    "pediatric" : false,
    "recommendation" : true,
    "relatedAlleles" : [],
    "relatedChemicals" : [
      {
        "objCls" : "Chemical",
        "id" : "PA131301952",
        "name" : "gefitinib",
        "version" : 20
      }
    ],
    "relatedGenes" : [
      {
        "objCls" : "Gene",
        "id" : "PA128",
        "symbol" : "CYP2D6",
        "name" : "cytochrome P450 family 2 subfamily D member 6",
        "version" : 7891
      }
    ],
    "source" : "DPWG",
    "summaryMarkdown" : {
      "id" : 1450414927,
      "html" : "<p>The Dutch Pharmacogenetics Working Group Guideline for gefitinib recommends to determine the trough concentration of gefitinib for CYP2D6 ultrarapid metabolizers and increase the dose or choose an alternative if the trough concentration is below 200 Âµg/l.</p>\\n",
      "version" : 1
    },
    "terms" : [],
    "textMarkdown" : {
      "id" : 1450414928,
      "html" : "<h3 id=\\"april-2026-guideline-update\\">April 2026 Guideline update</h3>\\n<p>The Royal Dutch Pharmacists Association - Pharmacogenetics Working Group (<a href=\\"/page/dpwg\\">DPWG</a>) released an updated version of the <a download=\\"pharmacogenetic_recommendation_text_20250501_downloaded042726.pdf\\" href=\\"https://api.clinpgx.org/v1/download/file/attachment/pharmacogenetic_recommendation_text_20250501_downloaded042726.pdf\\">Pharmacogenetic_recommendation_text</a> dated with 20250501. It includes CYP2D6-gefitinib guideline updates which are dated within the document as 27-01-2025.</p>\\n<p>DPWG has evaluated therapeutic dose recommendations for gefitinib based on CYP2D6 genotypes and conclude that no action is required for PM and IM phenotypes. For CYP2D6 UMs, it is recommended to determine the trough concentration of gefitinib and increase the dose or choose an alternative if the trough concentration is below 200 Âµg/l.</p>\\n<p><em>Wording in table taken from the DPWG <a download=\\"pharmacogenetic_recommendation_text_20250501_downloaded042726.pdf\\" href=\\"https://api.clinpgx.org/v1/download/file/attachment/pharmacogenetic_recommendation_text_20250501_downloaded042726.pdf\\">Pharmacogenetic_recommendation_text</a> accessed 04272026</em></p>\\n<table class=\\"table\\">\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>ALLELE/GENOTYPE/PHENOTYPE</th>\\n<th>DRUG</th>\\n<th>DESCRIPTION</th>\\n<th>RECOMMENDATION</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td>CYP2D6 PM</td>\\n<td>gefitinib</td>\\n<td>The gefitinib plasma concentration may increase due to reduced CYP2D6 activity. However, there is no evidence to suggest that side effects increase to an extent that adjustment of therapy is needed.</td>\\n<td>NO action is needed</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>CYP2D6 IM</td>\\n<td>gefitinib</td>\\n<td>Side effects can occur more frequently, as the gene variation increases the gefitinib plasma concentration. However, the side effects are reversible and manageable, to an extent that adjustment of the therapy in advance is not necessary. Furthermore, there is insufficient evidence to suggest that effectiveness is diminished.</td>\\n<td>NO action is needed</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>CYP2D6 UM</td>\\n<td>gefitinib</td>\\n<td>On theoretical grounds, there is an increased risk of the drug being ineffective. Genetic variation increases the activity of CYP2D6, one of the enzymes that converts gefitinib into a much less active metabolite.</td>\\n<td>Determine the trough concentration of gefitinib and increase the dose or choose an alternative if the trough concentration is below 200 Âµg/l. Erlotinib is not metabolised by CYP2D6.</td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody>\\n</table>\\n<p><a download=\\"DPWG_CYP2D6-gefitinib_4634-4636.pdf\\" href=\\"https://api.clinpgx.org/v1/download/file/attachment/DPWG_CYP2D6-gefitinib_4634-4636.pdf\\">Read for more information about this recommendation</a></p>\\n<h4 id=\\"preemptive-genotyping\\">Preemptive genotyping</h4>\\n<p>Excerpts from the <a download=\\"DPWG_CYP2D6-gefitinib_4634-4636.pdf\\" href=\\"https://api.clinpgx.org/v1/download/file/attachment/DPWG_CYP2D6-gefitinib_4634-4636.pdf\\">DPWG risk analysis document</a> for gefitinib and CYP2D6:</p>\\n<blockquote class=\\"blockquote\\">\\n<p>The KNMP Pharmacogenetics Working Group considers genotyping before starting gefitinib to be potentially beneficial for drug efficacy. Genotyping can be considered on an individual patient basis. If, however, the genotype is available, the KNMP Pharmacogenetics Working Group recommends adhering to the gene-drug guideline.</p>\\n</blockquote>\\n<p><a href=\\"/page/dpwgPreemptiveGenotyping\\">Read more about how DPWG assigns their recommendations for preemptive genotyping.</a></p>\\n",
      "version" : 8
    },
    "version" : 10
  }
}');
