      }
    ],
    "literature" : [
      {"id":15333034,"title":"Clinical Pharmacogenetics Implementation Consortium (CPIC) Guideline for CYP2D6 Genotype and Use of 5-HT 3 Receptor Antagonists: 2026 Update.","_sameAs":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/41979467","crossReferences":[{"id":1454744539,"resource":"PubMed","resourceId":"41979467","_url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/41979467"},{"id":1454744540,"resource":"DOI","resourceId":"10.1002/cpt.70291","_url":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1002%2Fcpt.70291"}],"objCls":"Literature","pubDate":"2026-04-01T00:00:00-07:00","terms":[{"id":1454108620,"resource":"ClinPGx Tags","term":"CPIC","termId":"pgkbTags:1454108620"},{"id":1451577480,"resource":"PGx Paper Types","term":"Implementation","termId":"pgxPaperTypes:1451577480"}],"type":"Literature"}
    ],
    "otherPrescribingGuidance" : false,
    "pediatric" : false,
    "recommendation" : false,
    "relatedAlleles" : [],
    "relatedChemicals" : [
      {
        "objCls" : "Chemical",
        "id" : "PA449390",
        "name" : "dolasetron",
        "version" : 8
      },
      {
        "objCls" : "Chemical",
        "id" : "PA10352",
        "name" : "palonosetron",
        "version" : 9
      },
      {
        "objCls" : "Chemical",
        "id" : "PA166365201",
        "name" : "ramosetron",
        "version" : 2
      }
    ],
    "relatedGenes" : [
      {
        "objCls" : "Gene",
        "id" : "PA128",
        "symbol" : "CYP2D6",
        "name" : "cytochrome P450 family 2 subfamily D member 6",
        "version" : 7891
      }
    ],
    "source" : "CPIC",
    "summaryMarkdown" : {
      "id" : 1454746000,
      "html" : "<p>There are currently no recommendations for dosing of dolasetron, palonosetron, or ramosetron based on CYP2D6 genotypes.</p>\\n",
      "version" : 0
    },
    "terms" : [],
    "textMarkdown" : {
      "id" : 1454746001,
      "html" : "<h3 id=\\"june-2026\\">June 2026</h3>\\n<ul>\\n<li>The authors of the &quot;Clinical Pharmacogenetics Implementation Consortium (CPIC) Guideline for CYP2D6 Genotype and Use of 5-Â­HT3 Receptor Antagonists: 2026 Update&quot; in <a rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\" href=\\"https://ascpt.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/cpt.70291\\" target=\\"_blank\\"><em>Clinical Pharmacology and Therapeutics</em></a> evaluated the available evidence for the use of ondansetron, tropisetron, dolasetron, palonosetron and ramosetron based on <em>CYP2D6</em> genotypes. They conclude that there is insufficient evidence to provide a recommendation for dolasetron, palonosetron and ramosetron based on <em>CYP2D6</em> genotypes at this time.</li>\\n<li>Excerpt from the 2026 ondansetron dosing guideline:\\n<ul>\\n<li>&quot;Although dolasetron, palonosetron, and ramosetron are also metabolized by CYP2D6 (Table S2), insufficient evidence are available regarding the effect on nausea and vomiting (Tables S3 and S4) (CPIC level C -Â­ no recommendation).&quot;</li>\\n</ul>\\n</li>\\n<li>Download and read:\\n<ul>\\n<li><a rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\" href=\\"https://files.cpicpgx.org/data/guideline/publication/ondansetron/2026/41979467.pdf\\" target=\\"_blank\\">Clinical Pharmacogenetics Implementation Consortium (CPIC) Guideline for CYP2D6 Genotype and Use of 5-Â­HT3 Receptor Antagonists: 2026 Update</a></li>\\n<li><a rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\" href=\\"https://files.cpicpgx.org/data/guideline/publication/ondansetron/2026/41979467-supplement.pdf\\" target=\\"_blank\\">2026 supplement</a></li>\\n</ul>\\n</li>\\n</ul>\\n",
      "version" : 0
    },
    "version" : 0
  }
}');
INSERT INTO guideline_raw (pharmgkb_id, json_data) VALUES ('PA166436801', '{
  "citations" : [],
  "guideline" : {
    "objCls" : "Guideline Annotation",
    "id" : "PA166436801",
    "name" : "Annotation of DPWG Guideline for sacituzumab govitecan and UGT1A1",
    "alternateDrugAvailable" : false,
    "cancerGenome" : false,
    "crossReferences" : [],
    "dosingInformation" : false,
    "hasTestingInfo" : true,
    "history" : [
      {
        "id" : 1454748463,
        "date" : "2026-04-27T00:00:00-07:00",
        "description" : "added based on pharmacogenetic_recommendation_text_20250501",
        "type" : "Update",
        "version" : 0
      },
      {
        "id" : 1454748502,
        "date" : "2026-04-27T13:18:10.657-07:00",
        "description" : "Published on ClinPGx.org",
        "type" : "Publish",
        "version" : 0
      }
    ],
    "literature" : [
      {"id":15333442,"title":"Dutch Pharmacogenetics Working Group Guidelines April 2026","_sameAs":"https://api.clinpgx.org/v1/preview/download/file/attachment/pharmacogenetic_recommendation_text_20250501_downloaded042726.pdf","crossReferences":[{"id":1454748320,"resource":"URL","resourceId":"https://api.clinpgx.org/v1/preview/download/file/attachment/pharmacogenetic_recommendation_text_20250501_downloaded042726.pdf","_url":"https://api.clinpgx.org/v1/preview/download/file/attachment/pharmacogenetic_recommendation_text_20250501_downloaded042726.pdf"}],"objCls":"Literature","terms":[{"id":1452267780,"resource":"ClinPGx Tags","term":"Has PGx","termId":"pgkbTags:1452267780"}],"type":"Literature"}
    ],
    "otherPrescribingGuidance" : true,
    "pediatric" : false,
    "recommendation" : true,
    "relatedAlleles" : [],
    "relatedChemicals" : [
      {
        "objCls" : "Chemical",
        "id" : "PA166225061",
        "name" : "sacituzumab govitecan",
        "version" : 4
      }
    ],
    "relatedGenes" : [
      {
        "objCls" : "Gene",
        "id" : "PA420",
        "symbol" : "UGT1A1",
        "name" : "UDP glucuronosyltransferase 1 family, polypeptide A1",
        "version" : 6110
      }
    ],
    "source" : "DPWG",
    "summaryMarkdown" : {
      "id" : 1454748460,
      "html" : "<p>The Dutch Pharmacogenetics Working Group Guideline for sacutuzumab govitecan recommends to be particularly vigilant for the occurrence of side effects in patients with the UGT1A1 *28/*28 genotype or UGT1A1 poor metabolizer phenotype.</p>\\n",
      "version" : 0
    },
    "terms" : [],
    "textMarkdown" : {
      "id" : 1454748461,
      "html" : "<h3 id=\\"april-2026-guideline\\">April 2026 Guideline</h3>\\n<p>The Royal Dutch Pharmacists Association - Pharmacogenetics Working Group (<a href=\\"/page/dpwg\\">DPWG</a>) released an updated version of the <a download=\\"pharmacogenetic_recommendation_text_20250501_downloaded042726.pdf\\" href=\\"https://api.clinpgx.org/v1/download/file/attachment/pharmacogenetic_recommendation_text_20250501_downloaded042726.pdf\\">Pharmacogenetic_recommendation_text</a> dated with 20250501. It includes UGT1A1-sacutuzumab govitecan guidelines which are dated within the document as 27-01-2025.\\nDPWG has evaluated therapeutic dose recommendations for sacutuzumab govitecan based on UGT1A1 genotype and recommends to be particularly vigilant for the occurrence of side effects in patients with the UGT1A1 *28/*28 genotype or UGT1A1 poor metabolizer phenotype.</p>\\n<p><em>Wording in table taken from the DPWG <a download=\\"pharmacogenetic_recommendation_text_20250501_downloaded042726.pdf\\" href=\\"https://api.clinpgx.org/v1/download/file/attachment/pharmacogenetic_recommendation_text_20250501_downloaded042726.pdf\\">Pharmacogenetic_recommendation_text</a> accessed 04272026</em></p>\\n<table class=\\"table\\">\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>Allele/Genotype/Phenotype</th>\\n<th>Drug</th>\\n<th>Description</th>\\n<th>Recommendation</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td>UGT1A1 *1/*28</td>\\n<td>sacutuzumab govitecan</td>\\n<td>This genetic variant (*1/*28) is more common in Western populations than the so-called wild type (*1/*1). This means that the treatment is largely tailored to patients with this genetic variant. Adjusting the treatment is therefore not useful.</td>\\n<td>NO action is needed for this gene-drug interaction.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>UGT1A1 *28/*28</td>\\n<td>sacutuzumab govitecan</td>\\n<td>There are indications that serious adverse events (particularly haematological adverse events and, to a lesser extent, diarrhoea) occur more frequently and at an earlier stage in patients with this gene variant. The gene variant reduces the inactivation of the active metabolite SN-38.</td>\\n<td>Be particularly vigilant for the occurrence of side effects.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>UGT1A1 IM other</td>\\n<td>sacutuzumab govitecan</td>\\n<td>This gene variant (IM) is more common in Western populations than the so-called wild type (*1/*1). This means that the choice of treatment is largely tailored to patients with this gene variant. It is therefore not useful to adjust the choice of treatment.</td>\\n<td>NO action is needed for this gene-drug interaction.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>UGT1A1 PM other</td>\\n<td>sacutuzumab govitecan</td>\\n<td>There are indications that serious side adverse events (particularly haematological adverse events and, to a lesser extent, diarrhoea) occur more frequently and at an earlier stage in patients with a gene variant that has a similar effect on the UGT1A1 enzyme. This gene variant reduces the inactivation of the active metabolite SN-38.</td>\\n<td>Be particularly vigilant for the occurrence of side effects.</td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody>\\n</table>\\n<p><a download=\\"DPWG_UGT1A1-sacituzumab_govitecan_8510-8513.pdf\\" href=\\"https://api.clinpgx.org/v1/download/file/attachment/DPWG_UGT1A1-sacituzumab_govitecan_8510-8513.pdf\\">Read for more information about this recommendation</a></p>\\n<h4 id=\\"preemptive-genotyping\\">Preemptive genotyping</h4>\\n<p>Excerpts from the <a download=\\"DPWG_UGT1A1-sacituzumab_govitecan_8510-8513.pdf\\" href=\\"https://api.clinpgx.org/v1/download/file/attachment/DPWG_UGT1A1-sacituzumab_govitecan_8510-8513.pdf\\">DPWG risk analysis document</a> for sacituzumab govitecan and UGT1A1:</p>\\n<blockquote class=\\"blockquote\\">\\n<p>The KNMP Pharmacogenetics Working Group does not recommend genotyping of UGT1A1 before starting sacituzumab\\ngovitecan.</p>\\n</blockquote>\\n<p><a href=\\"/page/dpwgPreemptiveGenotyping\\">Read more about how DPWG assigns their recommendations for preemptive genotyping.</a></p>\\n",
      "version" : 0
    },
    "version" : 1
  }
}');
